commit 5df56d376735933b3fb6c0097f5984771afab276
Author: Marat K <phpcraftdream@gmail.com>
Date:   Sun Aug 2 11:55:20 2026 +0200

    fix(perf): PerClass gains #[repr(C)]; restores documented one-cache-line magazine layout (R32-5, task #496)
    
    PerClass (src/registry/tcache.rs -- the per-size-class magazine: count +
    slots, and virgin_mask under virgin-zero-skip) had no #[repr(C)], so it
    used Rust's unspecified default layout. Its own doc comment (PERF-PASS-5,
    task #53) claims count sits "directly adjacent to (in front of)" slots so
    a magazine push/pop touches one 64-byte cache line instead of two.
    
    Independently re-verified via a scratch rustc -O + std::mem::offset_of!
    probe (not trusting the F4 survey finding blindly): rustc's default
    field-reordering heuristic put the 8-aligned slots array FIRST and count
    LAST -- offset_of(count) == 128, offset_of(slots) == 0 (136, with
    virgin-zero-skip: count at 130, virgin_mask at 128). For the documented
    common case (shallow magazine, count 1-3), count and slots[0] were always
    in different 64-byte lines. The claimed optimization was not in effect.
    
    Fix: added #[repr(C)] and reordered the DECLARED fields to count,
    virgin_mask (cfg-gated), slots -- under repr(C)'s declaration-order
    guarantee this puts the small fields first and pads slots to its own
    8-byte alignment right after them. Pinned with three compile-time
    const _: () = assert!(core::mem::offset_of!(...) == N, ...) checks
    (mirroring the file's existing TCACHE_CAP <= 16 assert) so a future field
    reorder or an accidental repr(C) removal fails the build instead of
    silently regressing the documented locality claim again.
    
    Post-fix: offset_of(count) == 0, offset_of(virgin_mask) == 2 (when
    present), offset_of(slots) == 8, in both feature configurations. Struct
    size unchanged at 136 bytes either way. count now shares a 64-byte line
    with slots[0..6] for 7 of every 8 classes, versus 0 of 8 before.
    
    Measurement (WSL/callgrind, isolated git worktree at this task's base
    commit 62e217fa1ca599d5903fb519c16ab9f0af55a7e0 for BEFORE, no bench-file
    changes needed -- the pre-existing alloc_magazine_prefill_only_16b /
    _hit_only_16b and alloc_zeroed_magazine_prefill_only_16b / _hit_only_16b
    pairs already isolate exactly the magazine hit/push path):
    
      isolated 16-hit magazine-pop delta (plain alloc, production):        0 Ir
      isolated 16-hit magazine-pop delta (alloc_zeroed, virgin-zero-skip):  0 Ir
    
    Exactly matches the F4 survey entry's own prediction ("expect 0 Ir delta
    -- same instructions, different addresses"). Every SeferAlloc-side
    absolute Ir number (small_churn_16b, churn_256b, aligned_churn_640b_a128)
    also moved by a uniform +755/+804 Ir (production/virgin-zero-skip) --
    investigated and attributed to the one-time HeapCore::new() zero-init
    codegen shift (PerClass::new() x 49 classes), not a per-op cost: three
    structurally different churn benches move by the EXACT SAME constant
    within each feature set (asserted by the derive script), and mimalloc's
    own benches in the same log runs are byte-identical between BEFORE/AFTER.
    
    This lands on documentation-correctness grounds (restores an
    already-decided task #53 invariant at zero size/Ir cost, now enforced by
    compile-time assert instead of aspirational), not a measured speedup --
    hence fix(perf), not perf(runtime)/perf(opt-in), per CLAUDE.md's
    commit-prefix taxonomy.
    
    Correctness: cargo test --features production (full tree) and cargo test
    --features "production,virgin-zero-skip" (full tree) both green. cargo
    fmt --check clean. cargo clippy --lib --tests --benches -D warnings clean
    under production, production+virgin-zero-skip, and --all-features.
    virgin-zero-skip alone (no alloc-global) cannot build the integration
    test tree (needs alloc-global for SeferAlloc/registry) -- confirmed
    pre-existing, unrelated to this diff.
    
    Raw logs + checked-script-derived (self-asserting) summary CSV:
    docs/perf/_raw_r496_repr_c_{before,after}_{production,virginzeroskip}.log,
    docs/perf/R496_PERCLASS_REPR_C_LAYOUT_FIX_GATE_summary.csv,
    scripts/r496_perclass_repr_c_summary.mjs. Full writeup:
